{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "Maintainer Architecture Overview",
  "description": "A maintainer walkthrough of the develop branch, from provider configuration through collection, analysis, and Markdown reports.",
  "ref": "develop",
  "isPrimary": true,
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "README.md",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "Project Flow",
      "description": "**Situation:** This CLI collects AI news and writes Markdown reports.\n\n**Mechanism:** RSS/Atom entries are filtered and deduplicated, linked HTML is preferred as analysis input, and an LLM produces a summary, category, and literacy level.\n\n**Implication:** Maintain behavior by following the data contract from `Article` through `AnalysisResult`, rather than changing an isolated stage.\n\n**Gotcha:** The application supports OpenAI-compatible cloud providers as well as local llama.cpp; it is not local-only."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/ai_info_collector/settings.py",
      "line": 14,
      "title": "Provider Configuration Loading",
      "description": "**Situation:** Configuration is split between common settings and provider-specific TOML files.\n\n**Mechanism:** The active `config/<provider>.toml` and the llama.cpp fallback configuration are merged into `analysis` before validation.\n\n**Implication:** Adding an OpenAI-compatible provider normally starts with configuration rather than a new backend class.\n\n**Gotcha:** A missing active-provider TOML means no compatible settings object is created."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/ai_info_collector/domain.py",
      "selection": {"start": {"line": 35, "character": 1}, "end": {"line": 55, "character": 1}},
      "title": "Configuration Contract",
      "description": "**Situation:** This block defines local llama.cpp settings, shared OpenAI-compatible settings, and provider selection.\n\n**Mechanism:** Provider-named extra fields are validated as `OpenAICompatibleSettings`, while local GGUF settings remain explicitly typed as `llama_cpp`.\n\n**Implication:** A new compatible provider can use the existing backend contract.\n\n**Gotcha:** Relative GGUF paths are resolved only for llama.cpp settings."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/ai_info_collector/cli.py",
      "selection": {"start": {"line": 23, "character": 1}, "end": {"line": 37, "character": 1}},
      "title": "Backend Selection and Fallback",
      "description": "**Situation:** `_create_analyzer()` decides which LLM serves each run.\n\n**Mechanism:** A configured cloud provider is used only when its environment variable is set; otherwise the CLI logs a warning and selects llama.cpp.\n\n**Implication:** Provider changes must preserve this centralized fallback behavior.\n\n**Gotcha:** Missing cloud credentials require a valid `config/llama_cpp.toml` and local runtime."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/ai_info_collector/collection.py",
      "selection": {"start": {"line": 73, "character": 1}, "end": {"line": 110, "character": 1}},
      "title": "Article Content Preference",
      "description": "**Situation:** Feed summaries can omit facts needed for analysis.\n\n**Mechanism:** Each fresh, deduplicated article page is fetched and extracted HTML is preferred over feed `content` or `summary`.\n\n**Implication:** Collection changes affect both analysis quality and prompt size.\n\n**Gotcha:** Page failures are nonfatal; only entries lacking both page and feed content are skipped."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/ai_info_collector/analysis.py",
      "selection": {"start": {"line": 55, "character": 1}, "end": {"line": 83, "character": 1}},
      "title": "OpenAI-Compatible Backend",
      "description": "**Situation:** Cloud providers share one backend implementation.\n\n**Mechanism:** The backend creates an OpenAI client from TOML settings and conditionally requests strict JSON output.\n\n**Implication:** Routing models such as `openrouter/free` work through configuration alone.\n\n**Gotcha:** Providers that do not guarantee strict JSON must set `json_response_format = false`; the analyzer still validates the response."
    },
    {
      "file": "src/ai_info_collector/pipeline.py",
      "selection": {"start": {"line": 24, "character": 1}, "end": {"line": 55, "character": 1}},
      "title": "Resilient Pipeline Policy",
      "description": "**Situation:** A source or article failure must not terminate the complete run.\n\n**Mechanism:** Collection, analysis, and filter errors are accumulated while successful results are limited by each source's `max_items`.\n\n**Implication:** Pipeline behavior can be tested using fake collectors and analyzers without models or network calls.\n\n**Gotcha:** Source names are quota keys, so duplicate names share a limit."
    },
    {
      "file": "tests/test_openai_compatible.py",
      "line": 34,
      "title": "Provider Regression Tests",
      "description": "**Situation:** Provider requests are verified without external API calls.\n\n**Mechanism:** A fake `openai` module captures client initialization and chat-completion arguments.\n\n**Implication:** Use this suite when changing model IDs, base URLs, credentials, or JSON mode.\n\n**Gotcha:** Provider-specific production response behavior still needs a manual integration check."
    },
    {
      "description": "You can now trace provider configuration into backend selection, article content into analysis, and failures into the final pipeline result.",
      "content": "## Use this map for safe changes\n\nYou can now trace provider configuration into backend selection, article content into analysis, and failures into the final pipeline result. Add provider changes with configuration and backend tests; add collection changes with collection and pipeline tests. Read `WINDOWS_SETUP.md` for local runtime setup and `CONTRIBUTING.md` for quality checks."
    }
  ]
}